# vLLM server / benchmark logs are tee'd to the console AND to this dir; never commit them
self-hosted/vllm/logs/
# Generated request, summary, and server-metric CSVs from the vLLM benchmark
# client, plus the throughput sweep's raw per-level JSONs and (large) DuckDB.
# EXCEPTION: commit each throughput run's performance-summary.json (the small,
# reproducible record) and its rendered performance-dashboard.html so the chart
# renders on GitHub. Re-include the dirs to reach them.
self-hosted/vllm/benchmark-output/**
!self-hosted/vllm/benchmark-output/
!self-hosted/vllm/benchmark-output/**/
!self-hosted/vllm/benchmark-output/**/performance-summary.json
!self-hosted/vllm/benchmark-output/**/performance-dashboard.html
# ...but never commit superseded/backup runs: the re-include above matches at any
# depth, so a local *-backup/ dir (e.g. a prior single-repo run kept for
# reference) would otherwise sneak in. Keep those local-only.
self-hosted/vllm/benchmark-output/**/*-backup/
.env
.env.*
.scratchpad/

# Benchmark run outputs. The large per-run design artifacts (github-issue/lld/
# review/testing .md, patch.diff, implementation.md) stay LOCAL -- they quote
# cloned third-party source and are bulky. COMMITTED per run: run-summary.json
# (the scrubbed rollup), plus per-task metrics.json (tokens/cost/turns + the
# normalized metrics block) and eval.json (judge scores + notes) so each run is
# fully inspectable and reproducible from git. To allow those files deep inside
# the ignored tree, the intervening directories are re-included.
benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**
# Re-include subdirectories (so git can descend) and the committed files.
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/*/
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**/
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/README.md
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**/run-summary.json
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**/metrics.json
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**/eval.json
# The Hello-World worked example is an intentional exception: its full artifacts
# (already committed) stay tracked so readers can see exactly what /swe produces.
# New real runs commit only run-summary.json per the rule above.
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**/Hello-World/**
# Per-task target-repo clones. The harness clones into
# <clone_dir>/swe-clone-<task-id>/ (clone_dir defaults to /tmp, outside the
# repo) and deletes them after each task; this ignore is a backstop for a config
# that points clone_dir inside the repo, so a leftover clone from a killed run
# can never be committed. The swe-clone- prefix is specific so this never
# matches the swe-benchmark-data output dir.
swe-clone-*/
**/swe-clone-*/
# Stray repo-root writes from throughput load sessions. The throughput harness
# runs `claude -p` with cwd=REPO_ROOT (the /swe2 slash command and root CLAUDE.md
# only resolve from there), so a load session that writes a BARE RELATIVE filename
# instead of the absolute artifacts_dir it was given drops the file here. The
# harness now sweeps these at the end of each level; this ignore is the backstop
# for names seen in the wild, so a killed run cannot leave one for `git add -A`.
/github-issue.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
credentials.json
.aws/
secrets/
security-review-findings.xlsx
.litellm.pid
.mantle-token
# HuggingFace token for gated/faster model downloads — never commit; consumed by vllm-serve.sh
.hf_token
**/.hf_token
.hftoken
**/.hftoken
.DS_Store
.venv/
tmp/
.claude/worktrees/
benchmarks/config/runner.yaml
# Proxy runtime artifacts (bearer token, pid, log) written by bedrock-mantle-proxy.sh
benchmarks/.mantle-token
benchmarks/.litellm.pid
benchmarks/.litellm.log
